// Bindings and back-references (docs/syntax.md §3.5.1): a text bound by `$q: X`, matched again
// by `$q`, and counted by `#q`. One grammar for each way a binding is read, so that the
// generated file shows each: the two positions a binding records, the comparison a reference
// makes with them, and the run-time bound of a count.

// ── The until scan, delimited and not ───────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `RawString` binds a run of quotes in an atomic group and scans to the same run again: the
// reference is a comparison of as many items as the opening had, at every position of the
// body. `LongString` reads its opening's `=` run the same way, but its scan tests a closing
// bracket first, so a near miss fails at its first item.

RawString  = { $q: '"'{3,} } & { (?!$q & any)* } & $q & ?!'"'
LongString = '[' & $eq: '='* & '[' & { (?!(']' & $eq & ']') & any)* } & ']' & $eq & ']'

// ── A binding that may be empty, and one shared by two routes ───────────────────────
//
// `$tag: (Tag?)` binds "" where there is no tag, so `$$ … $$` is the same rule. `Quoted`
// binds `t` on either route of the choice, and the reference after it reads whichever did.

DollarQuoted = '$' & $tag: (Tag?) & '$' & { (?!('$' & $tag & '$') & any)* } & '$' & $tag & '$'
Tag          = [\p{L} | '_'] & [\p{L} | \p{Nd} | '_']*
Quoted       = ('\'' & $t: Word & '\'' | $t: Word) & " " & $t
Word         = ['a'..'z']+

// ── Counts by a length ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `Heading` repeats `=` at least as many times as the title is long; `Between` reads both
// bounds of a count from two bindings, when the count is reached.

Heading = $t: Title & eol & '='{#t,} & eol
Title   = [^ '\r' | '\n']+
Between = $q: 'a'* & $r: 'c'* & ':' & 'b'{#q,#r}

// ── A binding per call ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `Element` calls itself between its tags; each call binds its own name, so the closing tag
// is compared with the opening of the same call.

Element = '<' & $n: Word & '>' & (Element | Text)* & "</" & $n & '>'
Text    = { [^ '<']+ }

// ── Beside members ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// A binding is no member: `Pair` has the two captures it names, and the reference is read
// as a capture's text like any other operand.

Pair : @string = c: ($q: Word) & ' ' & r: $q => @(c + "|" + r)

parse RawString
parse LongString
parse DollarQuoted
parse Quoted
parse Heading
parse Between
parse Element
parse Pair
find RawString as AnyRawString
